# Docker build context exclusions for veysl.de.
#
# Two jobs: (1) keep the build context small/fast, (2) never let runtime data
# leak into an image layer. (2) is the important one — Next.js's output file
# tracing for `output: 'standalone'` statically resolves the SQLite adapter's
# fallback path in payload.config.ts and will happily bundle whatever
# `veysl-cms.db` happens to sit in the build context straight into
# `.next/standalone/`. Confirmed locally: a build run next to the dev DB
# copied it byte-for-byte into the standalone output. Excluding it here means
# Next's tracer never sees it, so the image can never ship a customer's
# enquiry data or a stale test fixture. Production data lives only in the
# `veysl-data`/`veysl-media` named volumes (see docker-compose.yml).

# Dependencies (installed fresh inside the image)
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Next.js build output (produced inside the image)
.next
out

# Runtime data — SQLite DB + WAL/SHM sidecars, uploaded media
veysl-cms.db
veysl-cms.db-*
media

# Env files — secrets never enter the build context; compose passes them via
# env_file/build.args at deploy time instead
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control / editor / OS cruft
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Project docs/tooling not needed to build the app
.claude
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Deployment artifacts themselves (no reason to ship deploy/ or nginx/ inside
# the app image — they run on the host / in other containers)
deploy
nginx
.github

# Misc caches
.cache
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
